{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Requested the scope control that the identity question's registered discriminator asks for, so the third finding's outer boundary is measured rather than argued. The identity probe gains one case (`ok_is_truthful_when_the_entry_is_adopted`) and one transport facility (a list of dropped (sender, receiver) pairs); the original windowed case is unchanged. In the new case node 1 is leader and accepts its own entry at index 1 while both followers' receipts are dropped, so a quorum holds the entry yet node 1 stays at decided 0 with its call pending; node 2 then takes over, adopts the followers' log containing node 1's entry and decides index 1; the pairs are released and node 1 re-synchronizes. Locally both cases pass in 4.0s and the new case emits adopted_entry_resolution {a_decided_before: 0, a_decided_idx: 1, a_entry_at_index_1_is_own: true, b_decided_idx: 1, resolution: \\\"Ok(1)\\\"} — i.e. once the entry was adopted, Ok(1) is truthful, which bounds the false completion to entries that never reached a quorum (matching the adoption path through the prepare-phase Promise log_sync). Submission validated with execution requested. State of the audit: the event-backpressure finding is complete at every measured bound (8, 64 and the shipped default 1024) with the cluster-level stall and a corrected transport; the core accept-phase repair gap and the identity finding each hold with their receipts; the remaining limits are recorded per question (client-side trigger with no documented drain obligation for the event finding; only the 2-node configuration probed for the core gap; constructed interleaving plus cadence for the identity finding).\"}"}}
